# Optional GitHub token — SERVER-SIDE ONLY.
#
# Used by @fixly/core to read public repository manifests at a higher rate limit
# (unauthenticated GitHub allows ~60 requests/hour; a token raises this to
# ~5,000/hour). A classic token with no scopes, or a fine-grained token with
# public-repo read access, is sufficient. It is never exposed to the browser.
#
# Web app:    copy this file to apps/web/.env.local and fill in the value.
# Validation: export GITHUB_TOKEN in your shell before running `pnpm validate`.
GITHUB_TOKEN=
